{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"aa98294201430b3fb01e4f629eb02dbea8afbc9975da9332f632e6daccf0757d","digest":{"component_or_area":"rebar CLI read surfaces (show/list/search/ready)","key_entities":["_RECONVERGE_LOCK_TIMEOUT","ensure_fresh","src/rebar/_engine_support/reads.py","test_show_no_stall.py","test_reads_under_sync_contention.py","sync_contention_harness.py","_clear_sync_throttle","REBAR_SYNC_PUSH","/tmp/.ticket-sync-<md5>"],"problem_keywords":["concurrency","reads under contention","writer stall","output integrity","sync storm","reconverge lock","empty output"],"propositions":["Read CLI surfaces (show, list, search, ready) intermittently return empty stdout with exit 0 when reconverge lock times out under concurrent background auto-push writes.","The generic read-path property — exit 0 must produce parseable JSON of documented shape, valid-empty [] passes, truncated-empty fails — applies to all surfaces routing through ensure_fresh, not just show.","Throttle marker at /tmp/.ticket-sync-<md5(tracker)> gates reconverge to once per minute, so the harness must clear it before each parameterized read invocation to exercise the reconverge path instead of short-circuiting.","The ed2b fix (bounded reconverge lock timeout to 2s) is necessary but the property test must be generalized across all read surfaces to detect regressions on any of them, not just show."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787889803075298001,"uuid":"f80895c7-25e8-4f72-8946-0cc3f2c8579e"}